Privacy Policy

Introduction

Our privacy policy explains what information we collect at the service provider, how we use it, and what choices you have.
We built the application as a clinical follow-up system for healthcare providers. This service is provided by us and is intended for use as part of medical consultation workflows.

By using our service, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. The personal information we collect is used solely to provide and improve the service. We do not sell or share your information except as described in this Privacy Policy.

Information Collection and Use
To provide a better experience, we may collect personally identifiable information including but not limited to:

Patient name
Phone number
DOB
Gender
Medical consultation notes and history
Follow-up responses (e.g. “better”, “same”, “worse”)

This information is stored securely and used exclusively for clinical follow-up and communication purposes.

We may use third-party services (such as database and hosting providers) to support the operation of the application. These providers only process data on our behalf and are not permitted to use it for any other purpose.

WhatsApp Communication
We use the WhatsApp Cloud API to send follow-up messages to patients after a medical consultation.

These messages may include:

Post-consultation health check-ins
Follow-up reminders
Clinical status questions

Patients may respond using interactive WhatsApp buttons or messages. These responses are stored in our system to support clinical tracking and patient care.
Patients only receive WhatsApp messages after a consultation with a healthcare provider and as part of follow-up care.

Data Storage
All personal and medical data is securely stored using Supabase database infrastructure. We take appropriate security measures to protect data against unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.

Service Providers
We may use third-party companies and individuals to:

Provide and maintain the service
Process and store data
Send WhatsApp messages via the WhatsApp Cloud API
Monitor system performance

These providers are contractually obligated to protect your data and are not allowed to use it for any other purpose.

Security
We value your trust in providing personal information and use commercially acceptable means to protect it. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updates will be posted on this page and take effect immediately upon posting.

